    "updated_at": "2020-08-19T01:30:32Z",
    "body": "Hmm, I can rationalize opaque origins on the basis that `null != null`, even if this is not a property that is assumed.  But tuple origins that include domain are alone enough to invalidate the assumption.\r\n\r\nI can't remember where I saw this assumption being relied upon; it might be that the context can be relied upon for disambiguation in that case, but I'll have to look out for it now.",
